B2 then revealed row 4 and tapped its action while the keyboard toolbar was showing; no alert appeared. Its `blocked-diagnostic.png` (e20b4067â¦) shows the toolbar gone and row 4 still revealed: the tap was consumed dismissing the keyboard. The schedule `SectionList` sets no `keyboardShouldPersistTaps`, so React Native's default (`"never"`) applies to every control in the list (pre-existing since RN03). **Disposition:** not a swipe defect; recorded as an RN07 keyboard observation.

