## Tooling rules (lessons from RN03âRN05)

- Text evidence and handoffs use LF line endings (`.gitattributes` stores `migration/**` as LF). Disclose any CRLF capture; it needs a `-text` exception at commit time.
- Hermes headless may reject inline `node -e` / `python -c`: write `.mjs` helpers (spawnSync, argument arrays, no shell) in the run directory.
- Never trim git porcelain output: split raw stdout on `\n` and take paths from index 3.
- Before overwriting a file you read only in excerpts (this package's status line, a handoff), read it completely first, or write it with your own helper.
- An export inventory must come from the same run as the export receipt it is paired with.
- Stop on a failing check, record it honestly, and keep failed attempts as history.

